       mmqq__rreecceeiivvee() removes the oldest message with the highest priority from
       the message queue referred to by the message queue descriptor _m_q_d_e_s,
       and places it in the buffer pointed to by _m_s_g___p_t_r.  The _m_s_g___l_e_n argu‐
       ment specifies the size of the buffer pointed to by _m_s_g___p_t_r; this must
       be greater than or equal to the _m_q___m_s_g_s_i_z_e attribute of the queue (see
       mmqq__ggeettaattttrr(3)).  If _m_s_g___p_r_i_o is not NULL, then the buffer to which it
       points is used to return the priority associated with the received mes‐
       sage.

       If the queue is empty, then, by default, mmqq__rreecceeiivvee() blocks until a
       message becomes available, or the call is interrupted by a signal han‐
       dler.  If the OO__NNOONNBBLLOOCCKK flag is enabled for the message queue descrip‐
       tion, then the call instead fails immediately with the error EEAAGGAAIINN.

